## .NET Global Tool <small>(for developers)</small>

If you already have the [.NET 10 SDK](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download) installed, you can install Revela as a global tool. Revela is **not on NuGet.org yet**: download `Spectara.Revela.<version>.nupkg` (plus the plugin and theme `.nupkg` files you need) from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/releases) into a folder, then install from there:

```bash
dotnet tool install -g Spectara.Revela --version <version> --add-source ./revela-packages
revela config feed add releases /absolute/path/to/revela-packages
```

Update later by downloading the new packages into the same folder:

```bash
dotnet tool update -g Spectara.Revela --version <version> --add-source ./revela-packages
```

**Pick this if:** you already use .NET and want Revela on your `PATH`.

---

## Which one should I pick?

| | **Standalone** | **Full** | **.NET Tool** |
|---|---|---|---|
| Prerequisites | none | none | .NET 10 SDK |
| Download size | smallest | larger | smallest |
| Built-in plugins | all (fixed) | all (removable) | core only |
| Custom plugins | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Updates | manual download | manual download | `dotnet tool update` from downloaded packages |

When in doubt: **Standalone**, then follow [Your First Site](../../docs/get-started/first-site/). The [Installation guide](../../docs/get-started/installation/) covers every edition in detail, including updates and first-start warnings.
